{"author":"rebar-bridge[bot]","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1795261639370390002,"compiled_state":{"alias":"comic-heavyset-jerboa","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"5b14bafbc9e5017bc30ef4b5907d942e0db246ccb05268af931cedf6dfeb18dc","event_uuid":"9401ab2e-cf7a-4ac2-8c97-3f393e65220d","position":{"commit_sha":"c0a45f47c8c21ffdc11823b732799412cd76cff6","position":"1795261581107500001-9401ab2e-cf7a-4ac2-8c97-3f393e65220d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"56d555c3a1c7e6844cbd356eff01516c02735581a54bf4cf5bf91ad92441efa3","event_uuid":"6352e0cd-05e1-495a-958b-c6256a96465c","position":{"commit_sha":"51cff475c16f6bd7c81427f34dad79e1fef10cf3","position":"1795261617016158001-6352e0cd-05e1-495a-958b-c6256a96465c"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"7342c8a47c4cfc2e15ebe5004f7e3b295c9fc95c49fa8b6f2817b2a9d8a8ff54","event_uuid":"b6b636ca-e8a3-4dad-b9bf-a0cfe4119cb5","position":{"commit_sha":"6117cbd106c148df970cdac14484959642446934","position":"1795261639370390001-b6b636ca-e8a3-4dad-b9bf-a0cfe4119cb5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1795261581107500001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b6b636ca-e8a3-4dad-b9bf-a0cfe4119cb5","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"a2da-e61b-989e-4862"}],"description":"## Observation\nOn Windows, `git show <rev>:<path>` run without `--` dies with exit 128 and `fatal: failed to stat '<rev>:<path>': Filename too long` when the working directory plus the argument exceeds MAX_PATH. Git stats each revision argument as a possible filename to rule out ambiguity, and it aborts on any stat error other than ENOENT. Measured in Windows `sweep (windows)` diagnostic run 44899637411 (2026-11-21 PST): `fsck_restore`'s `git show <sha>^:<ticket>/<event>.json` failed this way under a pytest temp dir. The same test passed under a shorter temp path (run 44899366277). With `git cat-file blob` (which takes only an object name) it passed (run 44900309390). cold-censorable-armedcrab fixes the `fsck_restore` sites. This ticket covers the rest.\n\n## Sites on origin/main 1a11014a3a4 that read `<rev>:<path>` through `git show` with no `--`\n- src/rebar/_commands/_init_ensures.py:98, :122, :164 (`tickets:.gitattributes`, `tickets:.gitignore`, `tickets:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/init.py:440 (`tickets:.pre-commit-config.yaml`)\n- src/rebar/_commands/reclaim_publish.py:108 (`<rev>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:151 (`<tickets ref>:<path>`)\n- src/rebar/_opcert_gate_config.py:107 (`<spec>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/compat.py:180, :274 (`<remote ref>:<compat>`)\n- src/rebar/_store/project_ensures.py:67 (`tickets:<projects.json>`)\n- src/rebar/llm/evals/engine_comparison.py:217 (`HEAD:<path>`)\n\nBare-revision arguments, such as reclaim_eligibility.py:101 `show -s --format=%ct <sha>`, go through the same stat but are short enough to be unlikely to exceed the limit, so they are not listed. Several of the listed sites treat a non-zero exit as \"absent\", so a deep Windows path would misread an existing object as missing. One example is the `_init_ensures` units, which would then re-create and commit a file that exists.\n\n## Hypotheses (unproven per site)\nEvery site above can hit this on a deep enough Windows path. Short ref:path pairs under a shallow tracker path stay under MAX_PATH and never do.\n\n## Proposed direction\nRoute these reads through `git cat-file blob <rev>:<path>`, or add `--` after the revision, and add a regression test that drives each read with a cwd deep enough to exceed MAX_PATH on Windows.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"8c3d-a931-4c0b-4792","ticket_type":"bug","title":"git show <rev>:<path> dies with 'Filename too long' on deep Windows paths","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9401ab2e-cf7a-4ac2-8c97-3f393e65220d","6352e0cd-05e1-495a-958b-c6256a96465c","b6b636ca-e8a3-4dad-b9bf-a0cfe4119cb5"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795261639370390002,"uuid":"39939554-ac96-4831-8c76-fb8c468b1448"}